Full API spec:
All classes are declared in the default package (no package statement) and live directly under src/main/java. Public API and semantics:
- src/main/java/Bird.java:
  class Bird { Bird(double startY); double y(); double vy(); void applyGravity(); void integrate(); void flap(); }
  Semantics: y increases downward. Gravity adds +0.5 to vy and clamps vy to [-10.0, 10.0]. integrate() does y += vy. flap() overwrites vy = -8.0 regardless of current vy.
- src/main/java/RNG.java:
  class RNG { public final long originalSeed; RNG(long seed); long seed(); double nextDouble(); int nextInt(int bound); }
  Semantics: originalSeed stores constructor seed. seed() returns originalSeed without advancing internal java.util.Random. nextDouble()/nextInt(bound) delegate directly to the internal Random instance seeded in constructor.
- src/main/java/PipePair.java:
  class PipePair { PipePair(double x,double width,double gapY,double gapHeight,double speed); double x(); double width(); double gapY(); double gapHeight(); double speed(); boolean scored(); void markScored(); void move(); }
  Semantics: move() performs x -= speed each call. scored flag initially false; markScored() sets it true. Off-screen detection (x+width<0) is performed by Game, not exposed as API here.
- src/main/java/CollisionDetector.java:
  final class CollisionDetector { static boolean hitBounds(Bird bird, double birdHeight, double worldHeight); static boolean hitPipe(Bird bird, double birdWidth, double birdHeight, PipePair pipe, double worldHeight); }
  Semantics: hitBounds returns true if bird is outside vertical bounds using unclamped y and y+birdHeight. hitPipe determines collision against pipe using vertical overlap rules: top overlap when bird.y() < pipe.gapY() && bird.y()+birdHeight > 0.0; bottom overlap when bird.y() < worldHeight && bird.y()+birdHeight > pipe.gapY() + pipe.gapHeight(). Horizontal considerations (birdX vs pipe rectangle) are handled in Game; no comparisons of any y against pipe.x().
- src/main/java/ScoreSystem.java:
  final class ScoreSystem { static boolean passedPipe(double birdX, PipePair pipe); }
  Semantics: returns true exactly once when pipe.x() + pipe.width() < birdX and pipe is not yet scored; it calls pipe.markScored() to mark it. Subsequent calls for the same pipe return false.
- src/main/java/GameState.java:
  enum GameState { RUNNING, GAME_OVER }
- src/main/java/Game.java:
  class Game { Game(long seed); Game(long seed, double worldWidth, double worldHeight, int spawnInterval); boolean tick(); void reset(long seed); void flapBird(); double birdY(); double birdVy(); long ticks(); int score(); java.util.List<PipePair> pipes(); }
  Semantics: Game(seed) delegates to Game(seed, 400.0, 600.0, 100). Initializes state RUNNING, bird at y = worldHeight/2.0 with vy = 0.0, pipes empty, score 0, tickCount 0, and rng = new RNG(seed). Tick order while RUNNING: bird.applyGravity(); bird.integrate(); collision checks on resulting position without any additional clamping: first hitBounds(bird, 30.0, worldHeight), then for each pipe call hitPipe(bird, 30.0, 30.0, pipe, worldHeight). Per-pipe loop also checks scoring via ScoreSystem.passedPipe(birdX, pipe) before any off-screen removal. tick() increments internal tick counter exactly once per call; spawning occurs after increment when ticks % spawnInterval == 0. Default birdX and bird dimensions are constant inside Game; gravity/flap constants as specified. If any collision occurs, state transitions to GAME_OVER for that tick; tick() returns false thereafter. Otherwise tick() returns true when remaining in RUNNING; false when the state is GAME_OVER after applying the tick. reset(seed) restores RUNNING state, replaces rng with new RNG(seed), clears pipes, resets tickCount=0, score=0, bird at worldHeight/2.0 and vy=0.0; world dimensions and spawnInterval unchanged. flapBird() sets bird.flap() only if state is RUNNING; ignored if GAME_OVER. Accessors return current state values: birdY() returns bird.y(), birdVy() returns bird.vy(), ticks() returns tickCount, score() returns score, pipes() returns the current mutable list (non-null) managed by Game.
- src/main/java/Main.java:
  class Main { public static void main(String[] args); }
  Semantics: Constructs a Game with a seed (any deterministic long), performs one standalone call game.tick(); ignores its boolean result; then prints in order: birdY(), birdVy(), ticks(), score(), and pipes().size(). No GUI. No external dependencies beyond JUnit Jupiter in tests.
Import/usage rules: Tests and Main instantiate and use only the APIs declared above. All classes reside in the default package and are referenced by simple class names. Callers must not invent aliases or alternate signatures. Tick order, gravity, flap, velocity clamp, scoring, collision rules, and spawn timing must strictly follow the stated fixtures.
